"""

         Outgoing-Packet Repetition Matching
         + Granular Computing with Rough Sets
================================================================
Directional reduction: only outgoing repeated packets sharing the
same destination and port are compared. Fusion with multi-granularity
rough sets at k = 2, 4, 8.

Fixes in this version:
  1. prep() drops ALL label-like columns (attack_cat, class, target,
     type, malicious, category, subcategory, flow_id, session_id, ...)
     to eliminate the perfect-1.0 tree-model leak seen on
     NIDS_Bench_2026.
  2. KAC-GR (all outgoing) simplified to k=4 only — k=8 over 27+
     features caused sparse granules and regression on some datasets.
  3. Granular Rough / Rough Set (ALONE) baselines use smaller
     min_granule_size / min_class_size so they stop collapsing to
     majority class on high-dimensional datasets.
  Plus (from previous version):
  * _norm() column-name normalisation.
  * Expanded alias tables for outgoing and stepping-stone features.
  * Diagnostic prints for KAC-feature collapse.

Outputs:
  paper2_kac_flat_rules.csv
  paper2_kac_gr_medium_rules.csv
  paper2_kac_gr_all_outgoing_rules.csv
  paper2_ssd_gr_rules.csv
  paper2_tiers.csv
  paper2_roc.png, paper2_pr.png, paper2_cm.png
  paper2_importance_*.png
"""

